    "",
    "  node run-bookings.js --limit 1",
    "  node statement-csv.js --rows statement-rows.json --bookings created-bookings.json --in-order --limit 1",
    "",
    "  Booking 1  hotel only, 150.00 (75.00 x 2 nights). No flight, no costing.",
    "     CSV row 1 is 150.00 -> settles the one segment exactly -> Allocated",
    "",
    "  NOTE: with a SINGLE segment, picking 'the only segment' is picking all of",
    "  them, so this goes down the proven Select All path. The per-segment",
    "  tick-then-type path only runs when a booking has more than one segment and",
    "  the receipt covers some of them — bookings 2 and 3 below do that.",
    "",
    "Bookings 2 and 3 are the fuller set, run with all six CSV rows:",
    "",
    "  booking 2  hotel  60.00, ticket 200.00",
    "     row 2  200.00  -> settles the ticket exactly        Allocated",
    "     row 5  100.00  -> settles the 60.00 hotel only      Part allocated",
    "",
    "  booking 3  hotel 790.00, ticket 250.00",
    "     row 3  200.00  -> nothing is small enough           Not allocated",
    "     row 6  790.00  -> settles the hotel exactly         Allocated",
    "",
    "THE HOTEL `rate` IS PER NIGHT — verified live on booking 13127, where rate",
    "100.00 over 2 nights produced Due inc GST 200.00. A segment's Debtor Due is",
    "rate x nights for the hotel, and the fare for the ticket.",
    "",
    "A receipt settles WHOLE segments only, picking the combination whose total is",
    "the largest that does not exceed it.",
    "",
    "clientCode must already exist in Tramada (SURNAME/FIRSTNAME), and creditor",
    "must be a real Tramada creditor — an unmatched one stops the run and asks."
  ],
